############################################################
# Local development only.
#
# Copy this file to requirements-local.txt (gitignored) in this same
# directory, and edit the three paths below to point at YOUR OWN local
# clones of these private (GemminAI-internal) repositories.
#
# Never commit requirements-local.txt.
# Never put a real path in this .example file.
#
# meaning-mapper, meaning-space-runtime, and categorical-lift-engine are
# not published to PyPI or any public index -- they must be cloned
# separately (private GitHub access required) and referenced here as
# editable installs for local iteration on this service.
#
# categorical-lift-engine is only needed for tests/e2e/ (Phase 3's minimal
# MeaningMapper -> MSR -> CLE -> hekb-vnext loop) -- runtime.services.
# meaning_trajectory (this service's own production code) does not import
# cle at all, only meaning_mapper and msr.
#
# Install with:
#   pip install -r requirements.txt -r requirements-local.txt
#
# Known gap, disclosed rather than silently worked around: this
# repository does not yet define how a container/production build is
# meant to obtain these packages (no private package index, no
# build-context vendoring is configured anywhere in this repo as of this
# note). services/nvs-runtime/Dockerfile currently installs only from
# requirements.txt and will not have MeaningMapper/meaning-space-runtime
# available at runtime until that mechanism exists.
############################################################

-e /path/to/your/local/clone/of/meaning-mapper
-e /path/to/your/local/clone/of/meaning-space-runtime
-e /path/to/your/local/clone/of/categorical-lift-engine
